  "lineage": "Mid-1990s Chicago electronic subgenre developed as faster-tempo evolution of Chicago ghetto house, characterized by extreme-tempo (155-165 BPM), syncopated drum-machine programming, chopped-vocal sampling, and explicit footwork-dance-battle functional context. Distinguished from later footwork by juke's simpler structural framework. DJ Deeon, DJ Funk, and the Dance Mania Records label (founded 1985) anchored the canonical juke transition into footwork.",
